[LESSON]: Counterexamples in Alloy RBAC models often indicate underspecified state transitions or insufficient cardinality/role constraints. Assertions that pass vacuously (e.g., because transitions never occur) should be guarded against by additional reachability or scenario-enforcing assertions.

[EVENT]: Detected model allows Emergency to be entered from non-Normal states and with incorrect emAdmins; prescribed strengthening of Emergency entry constraints and administrator cardinality checks.

[EVENT]: Found model does not reliably enforce mutual exclusion suspension only during Emergency; suggested concrete strengthening of MutualExclusionEnforced fact and related role assignment logic.

[EVENT]: Identified that credential update and delegation revocation requirements are not precisely enforced post-Emergency; recommended making these sets exactly match emAdmins and Emergency-assigned delegations only.
